course: dictionary
lesson: 11952
title: Word meanings in context: cardigan
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A cardigan is a knitted jumper that opens down the front. You can tell because it does up with buttons or a zip. «Sam put on his cardigan before he went out into the cold.» You put a cardigan on like a jumper, so it is a piece of clothing.
explain: Look for the clues around the word. «Mia did up all the buttons on her cardigan.» Buttons, and the words did up, tell you that the cardigan opens at the front. Always check your meaning by putting it into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
explain: Some clues tell you where a cardigan is worn. «Everyone in Year 5 wore their navy school cardigan on the trip.» A school cardigan is a cardigan worn as part of school uniform, so you can see it is warm clothing worn at school.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Cardigan» means a knitted jumper that opens down the front.
fact: A cardigan does up with buttons or a zip.
fact: «Cardigan» is a noun, a name for a thing: a cardigan, two cardigans.
exercise: Sam's grandad wears a warm grey «cardigan» every winter. What is a cardigan? | *A knitted jumper that opens down the front | A pair of wellies for muddy fields | A hat for the snow | A pair of trousers with big pockets
exercise: «Mia did up all the buttons on her cardigan.» What does did up mean? | Washed | Took off | Tore | *Fastened
exercise: «Put on your cardigan, it is chilly outside.» Find and copy the word that names the warm clothing. | chilly | *cardigan | put | outside
test: «Put on your cardigan, it is chilly outside.» What does cardigan mean? | *A knitted jumper that opens down the front | A raincoat with a hood | A pair of gloves | A long, flowing dress
test: Ella asks, «How does a cardigan fasten?» What is the answer? | *Buttons or a zip | A hook on the back | Laces | Velcro only
exam: «Grandma knitted a new cardigan for my birthday.» What does knitted tell you about the cardigan? | It was ironed flat | *It was made by knitting, using needles and yarn | It was bought from a shop with a zip | It was painted blue
